      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c62e995865713647a7115b|full_name}: In my case I was originally trying to set up something where I could adjust parameters in real time to better understand what they do. If this isn't intended to be supported, please put a note to this effect in the documentation.\n\nNote also that I was specifically animating the VoiceOverrideRegion parameters, not the collider itself.\n\nAnimating the enable/disable state itself, or moving the collision region, would be useful as it can be used to simulate more complex behavior - eg having two rooms side by side but preventing you from hearing the other side by forcing the far range to zero for the room you're not in, or having a small region follow a specific player.. Last I tested, animating enable/disable state worked, but I haven't tested moving the region.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
