  "details": "Test world ID: wrld_03f17561-5b91-4472-90e6-4ef148da2d6b\n\nIt appears that, if you adjust the values on a VRC_Voice Override Region with an animator, the new values are not consistently applied.\n\nThe test world has a number of sandbox platforms for exploring the new component, but in particular it has two platforms that switch between a far range of 50 and 0, one of which turns off the object with the voice override region between changes. One simply changes the values, while the other disables the game object containing the component before changing values, then re-enables it. In the case where the component is not disabled, the changes do not seem to have effect. When it is disabled, sometimes it seems to take effect, but it appears to be inconsistent.\n\nSummary in Japanese (for the benefit of folks who helped test):\n\nVRC_Voice Override Regionの設定値をアニメーターで操作した場合、新しい値が適用されない場合があるようです。\n\nこのテストワールドでは新しいコンポーネントの検証用の台がありますが、特にfar値を50と0で切り替える第が二つあります。片方は単に切り替えるだけですが、もう片方は切り替えるときコンポーネントがついているGameObjectを一旦無効化しています。無効化しないほうでは、新しい値が一切適用されないようですが、もう片方は適用される場合もあるようですが、かなり不安定のようです。",
